      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:3:92:3",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَمِيرُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ( عليه السلام ) شَرُّ بِئْرٍ فِي النَّارِ بَرَهُوتُ الَّذِي فِيهِ أَرْوَاحُ الْكُفَّارِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Muhammad Bin Ahmad, by a chain of his, said, ",
          "‘Amir Al-Momineen<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The most evil of the wells in the Fire is Barhout (a valley in Yemen) in which are the souls of the Infidels’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Muhammad ibn Ahmad through the chain of his narrators has said the following: “’Amir al-Mu’minin, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘The worst well in the fire is the well of Barahut in which the souls (spirits) of unbelievers live.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
